////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// Verification Scope
- reservoir_no_backpressure is intentionally derived from reservoir
- unchanged storage, occupancy, clock-enable, shifting, simultaneous fill/drain,
  reset, drain-data, drain-valid and drain-burstmark logic is verified in:
  rtl/memory_systems/reservoir/manual_verify.mv
- this file verifies only the small behavioral and interface differences from reservoir
[Marc103 - 08/13/26]

"
module reservoir_no_backpressure #(
    parameter DATA_WIDTH,
    parameter WATERMARK_ENTRIES,
    parameter FILLMARK,
    parameter BURSTMARK,

    ////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
    // Globally Defined Locally Set Parameters
    localparam ENTRIES = reservoir_ENTRIES(WATERMARK_ENTRIES, 0)
)
"
- DATA_WIDTH, WATERMARK_ENTRIES and BURSTMARK retain their reservoir meanings
- BACKPRESSURE_ENTRIES is intentionally removed because this implementation does not
  accept late valid entries after ready deasserts
- FILLMARK is added to describe how many free entries are required for fill-side burst
  admission
- reservoir_ENTRIES receives zero backpressure entries, so ENTRIES is exactly
  WATERMARK_ENTRIES
- the common reservoir storage logic therefore allocates only watermark entries
[Marc103 - 08/13/26]

"
    input clk_i,
    input rst_i,

    // Fill side
    input [DATA_WIDTH - 1 : 0] fill_data_i,
    input                      fill_valid_i,

    output                     fill_ready_o,
    output                     fill_burstready_o,

    // Drain side
    input                       drain_ready_i,

    output [DATA_WIDTH - 1 : 0] drain_data_o,
    output                      drain_valid_o,
    output                      drain_burstmark_o
"
- the original reservoir interface is retained except for fill_burstready_o
- fill_burstready_o allows an upstream producer to determine whether FILLMARK entries can
  be accepted as a complete burst
- fill_ready_o remains the single-entry ready signal used with fill_valid_i
- the drain-side interface is unchanged and remains covered by the reservoir verification
[Marc103 - 08/13/26]

"
    // Can't fill when reservoir is full
    assign fill = fill_valid_i & (!occupied[0]);
    // can't drain if the reservoir is empty.
    assign drain = occupied[ENTRIES - 1] & drain_ready_i;
"
- because ENTRIES equals WATERMARK_ENTRIES, occupied[0] is the top entry and indicates
  that every reservoir entry is occupied
- !occupied[0] is therefore equivalent to fill_ready_o in this implementation
- fill occurs only when fill_valid_i and fill_ready_o are both asserted, implementing the
  traditional valid/ready acceptance rule
- a valid held while full is not consumed repeatedly; it is accepted once space becomes
  available and ready asserts again
- drain behavior is unchanged from reservoir and remains covered by its manual verification
[Marc103 - 08/13/26]

"
    assign fill_ready_o = !occupied[ENTRIES - WATERMARK_ENTRIES];
    assign fill_burstready_o = !occupied[FILLMARK - 1];

    assign drain_data_o      = reservoir[ENTRIES - 1];
    assign drain_valid_o     = occupied[ENTRIES - 1];
    assign drain_burstmark_o = occupied[ENTRIES - BURSTMARK];
"
- ENTRIES equals WATERMARK_ENTRIES, so fill_ready_o indexes occupied[0] and asserts when
  the reservoir is not full
- occupied entries remain contiguous at the bottom of the reservoir, as verified for the
  original reservoir
- occupancy grows from occupied[WATERMARK_ENTRIES - 1] toward occupied[0]
- occupied[FILLMARK - 1] asserts when occupancy exceeds WATERMARK_ENTRIES - FILLMARK;
  its inversion therefore includes the boundary where exactly FILLMARK entries are free
- FILLMARK must be in [1, WATERMARK_ENTRIES] so the packed-array index remains valid
- drain_data_o, drain_valid_o and drain_burstmark_o are unchanged from reservoir
[Marc103 - 08/13/26]

////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// AI Verification Summary
- all unchanged reservoir state and datapath logic delegates to reservoir/manual_verify.mv
- no backpressure entries are allocated
- fill acceptance follows fill_valid_i && fill_ready_o
- fill_burstready_o reports capacity for FILLMARK entries
- drain behavior is unchanged
- parameter legality is not guarded locally and remains an integration requirement
[Marc103 - 08/13/26]
